// Entries use relaxed atomics so racy multi-threaded access is defined
// behaviour in Rust; on x86-64 these compile to plain loads and stores.

Aster changes (2026-10-19): lifetime-checked write leases, typed associative
cache storage, checked allocation/lookup, automatic thread-sharing traits,
and state/replacement/concurrency/lifetime regression checks.
